CBMC ignores alignas in struct layout (sizeof 1 instead of 4); the
libstdc++ __aligned_membuf pattern under std::map/std::unordered_set
nodes inherits the wrong layout.  Reduced from cpp20_map_basic via
cvise (valgrind-clean 32-line false positive on m[1] == 42).

FIXED 2026-07-18: three-part fix -- (1) parser.y's _Alignas(type)
action built the _Alignof on a discarded stack entry (C); (2) the C++
parser merged alignas into declaration.type() but rIntegralDeclaration
swapped it away; (3) the C++ front end neither folded the alignment
expression to a constant nor ran add_padding for explicitly-aligned
structs.
